\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Here, O my Lord, I see Thee face to face;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Here would I touch and handle things unseen,
\par Here grasp with firmer hand the eternal grace,
\par And all my weariness upon Thee lean.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Mine is the sin, but Thine the righteousness;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Mine is the guilt, but Thine the cleansing blood;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Here is my robe, my refuge, and my peace -
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Thy blood, thy righteousness, O Lord  my God.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Here would I feed upon the bread of God,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Here drink with thee the royal wine of heav'n;
\par Here would I lay aside each earthly load,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Here taste afresh the calm of sin forgiven.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. This is the hour of banquet and of song;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj This is the heavenly table spread for me;
\par Here let me feast, and, feasting, still prolong
\par This hallowed hour of fellowship with thee.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  Too soon we rise; the symbols disappear;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj The feast, though not the love, is past and gone;
\par The bread and wine remove, but thou art here,
\par Nearer than ever, still my Shield and Sun.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  I have no help but thine; nor do I need
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Another arm but thine to lean upon;
\par It is enough, my Lord, enough indeed;
\par My strength is in thy might, thy might alone.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Feast after feast thus comes and passes by,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Yet, passing, points to the glad feast above,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Giving sweet forestate of the festal joy,
\par \pard     The Lamb's great bridal feast of bliss and love.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

